<!--
  modules/terminal/pom.xml — Wave F module POM: the final-review CRITICAL finding
  (docs/design/build-cmake-maven-migration.md, Stage 2-f).

  STATUS: ADDITIVE and RUN BY HAND (mvn -pl modules/terminal -am package from the
  reactor root, or mvn -f modules/terminal/pom.xml package). Ant
  (modules/terminal/build.xml + build.incl.xml) remains the real build; nothing
  here is wired into CMake or any release build yet.

  WHY THIS MODULE, AND WHY IT IS NOT LIKE THE OTHER 23. `terminal` (the embedded
  JediTerm terminal, docs/design/terminal-live-reload.md) is a normal Java module
  — 7 source files, its own build.xml (default="jar", imports build.incl.xml) —
  and a genuinely SHIPPING one: etc/classpath.xml:286 loads
  org.scilab.modules.terminal.jar into the running application. Stage 2-f's own
  "DONE" report declared the reactor complete at 23/23, derived from
  prebuildjava/build.xml:25's hand-encoded topo-sort — but that list was never
  the right ground truth for "every module that ships": `terminal` is GUI-gated
  and built via its own USEANT=1 path (modules/terminal/Makefile.am:34), outside
  prebuildjava entirely, so it was never a candidate for any of Waves A-E and the
  23/23 claim was one module short. The build-parity completeness gate could not
  catch this either, by construction: it only ever asked "did every REACTOR
  module produce a jar" (one direction), never "does every Ant-built module jar
  have a reactor module" (the other) — see
  build-parity/tests/test_acceptance.py::_ant_modules_without_reactor_entry,
  added in the SAME change that adds this POM, and watched to fail naming
  `terminal` before this file existed. Previously tracked as orphan **B3** in
  docs/design/deferred-fixes-register.md; this POM resolves the Maven-reactor
  half of that row (the Ant-side fact — outside prebuildjava's topo-sort — is
  permanent and unaffected, per *reproduce, don't improve*).

  STEP 1 FINDINGS (./maven-module-deps.sh terminal, 7 files):
    [1] imports resolve to FOUR reactor dependencies, all already migrated:
          action_binding (InterpreterManagement — ScilabTerminal.java:54),
          commons ({,gui,xml}.* — ScilabConstants/ScilabGUIUtilities,
          ScilabTerminal.java:55-56; XConfiguration{,.XConfAttribute},
          TerminalOptions.java:20-21), gui (bridge.{console,tab,window},
          console, events.callback, menu{,bar,item}, tab, tabfactory, textbox,
          toolbar, utils — by far the widest single package family, spread
          across ScilabTerminal.java/TerminalTab.java/TerminalTabFactory.java),
          and localization (Messages — ScilabTerminal.java:78, the ordinary
          reactor-sibling idiom used across nearly every module). `localization`
          is not in this task's own dependency summary but IS a genuine direct
          import (confirmed: `import org.scilab.modules.localization.Messages;`
          is real code, ScilabTerminal.java:78, not a comment) — declared
          explicitly below, matching every other migrated module's own
          convention of listing a directly-imported reactor sibling even where
          it would also arrive transitively (e.g. modules/gui/pom.xml's own
          localization entry, needed despite commons already carrying it).
    [2] reflection targets — RULED OUT: org.scilab.modules.ui_data.FileBrowser
        is reached only via Class.forName("org.scilab.modules.ui_data.
        FileBrowser").getMethod("openFileBrowser").invoke(null)
        (ScilabTerminal.java:723), with the source's OWN comment stating the
        reason explicitly: "Invoked reflectively to avoid a compile-time
        dependency on the ui_data ... module". Reproduced as an absence, same
        shape as every other module's ruled-out Class.forName target.
    [3] fully-qualified uses with no import — none outside java.*.
  Vendored, on the established systemPath mechanism:
    - org.flexdock.docking.{Dockable, DockingConstants, DockingManager,
      DockingPort} (ScilabTerminal.java:49-52) — thirdparty/flexdock-1.2.5.jar,
      SAME MECHANISM, SAME COORDINATE AS modules/commons/pom.xml and
      modules/gui/pom.xml (cross-referenced, not restated).
    - com.jediterm.{core.util.TermSize, terminal.{TtyConnector,
      TerminalExecutorServiceManager}} — thirdparty/jediterm-core-3.70.jar;
      com.jediterm.terminal.ui.{JediTermWidget, settings.{DefaultSettingsProvider,
      SettingsProvider}} — thirdparty/jediterm-ui-3.70.jar. TWO jars, not one:
      `unzip -l` on both confirms the split (TtyConnector/
      TerminalExecutorServiceManager/TermSize live in -core; JediTermWidget/
      DefaultSettingsProvider/SettingsProvider live in -ui), and Maven's
      system-scope dependencies are never transitively resolved, so both must be
      declared even though jediterm-ui depends on jediterm-core upstream. Real
      Maven coordinates (not invented) sourced directly from
      fetch-thirdparty.sh's own MAVEN_MANIFEST heredoc: `org.jetbrains.jediterm:
      jediterm-core:3.70` / `org.jetbrains.jediterm:jediterm-ui:3.70` (repo "jb"
      = JetBrains' own intellij-dependencies repository, not Central) — same
      "real coordinate, system scope never resolves it" standing as
      modules/gui/pom.xml's gson/jcef-api entries. build.incl.xml:67-68
      (`${jediterm-core.jar}` / `${jediterm-ui.jar}`); scilab-lib.properties:70-71.
    - com.sun.jna.{Library, Memory, Native, Pointer, StringArray} and
      com.sun.jna.ptr.IntByReference (Pty.java:16-21, the PTY/JNI bridge) —
      thirdparty/jna-5.14.0.jar. Real Maven Central coordinate
      `net.java.dev.jna:jna:5.14.0`, same fetch-thirdparty.sh MAVEN_MANIFEST
      source as the pair above. build.incl.xml:74 (`${jna.jar}`);
      scilab-lib.properties:78.

  MANIFEST: a NORMAL per-package section (unlike javasci's bare-manifest
  exception, register B12) — extracted from the actual Ant-built jar's
  META-INF/MANIFEST.MF (unzip -p modules/terminal/jar/
  org.scilab.modules.terminal.jar META-INF/MANIFEST.MF), never retyped:
  Specification-Vendor and Implementation-Vendor both carry the double-mangled
  "Ã¨" (bytes c3 83 c2 a8), same mechanism as every other module (see
  modules/localization/pom.xml's fuller comment). Implementation-Version is
  present, frozen at the literal "00000000 0000" between Implementation-Title
  and Implementation-Vendor, exactly where Ant's own jar places it (Ant's live
  value there today is a DSTAMP/TSTAMP pair). Class-Path is the literal,
  never-interpolated string "${manifest.class-path}" — terminal's build.xml
  never defines the `manifest.class-path` property (confirmed: only
  `library.name` and `library.title` are set), so Ant leaves the reference
  unresolved and this fragment reproduces that literal text exactly, same
  standing as modules/localization/pom.xml and modules/action_binding/pom.xml.
-->
<project xmlns="http://maven.apache.org/POM/4.0.0"
         xmlns:xsi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance"
         xsi:schemaLocation="http://maven.apache.org/POM/4.0.0 http://maven.apache.org/xsd/maven-4.0.0.xsd">
  <modelVersion>4.0.0</modelVersion>

  <parent>
    <groupId>org.scilab</groupId>
    <artifactId>scilab-modules-parent</artifactId>
    <version>2027.0.0-SNAPSHOT</version>
    <relativePath>../../pom.xml</relativePath>
  </parent>

  <artifactId>terminal</artifactId>
  <packaging>jar</packaging>

  <!-- build.xml:17 <property name="library.title" value="Scilab terminal"/> -->
  <name>Scilab terminal</name>

  <dependencies>
    <!-- org.scilab.modules.action_binding.InterpreterManagement
         (ScilabTerminal.java:54). -->
    <dependency>
      <groupId>org.scilab</groupId>
      <artifactId>action_binding</artifactId>
      <version>${project.version}</version>
    </dependency>
    <!-- org.scilab.modules.commons.ScilabConstants,
         commons.gui.ScilabGUIUtilities (ScilabTerminal.java:55-56); commons.xml.
         XConfiguration and the static import XConfiguration.XConfAttribute
         (TerminalOptions.java:20-21). -->
    <dependency>
      <groupId>org.scilab</groupId>
      <artifactId>commons</artifactId>
      <version>${project.version}</version>
    </dependency>
    <!-- org.scilab.modules.gui.{bridge.console, bridge.tab, bridge.window,
         console, events.callback, menu, menubar, menuitem, tab, tabfactory,
         textbox, toolbar, utils} — this module's widest package family, across
         ScilabTerminal.java, TerminalTab.java and TerminalTabFactory.java. -->
    <dependency>
      <groupId>org.scilab</groupId>
      <artifactId>gui</artifactId>
      <version>${project.version}</version>
    </dependency>
    <!-- org.scilab.modules.localization.Messages (ScilabTerminal.java:78) — the
         ordinary reactor-sibling idiom used across nearly every module, declared
         explicitly despite also arriving transitively via commons/gui, matching
         modules/gui/pom.xml's own localization entry. -->
    <dependency>
      <groupId>org.scilab</groupId>
      <artifactId>localization</artifactId>
      <version>${project.version}</version>
    </dependency>
    <!-- FLEXDOCK — org.flexdock.docking.{Dockable, DockingConstants,
         DockingManager, DockingPort} (ScilabTerminal.java:49-52). SAME
         MECHANISM, SAME COORDINATE AS modules/commons/pom.xml and
         modules/gui/pom.xml (cross-referenced, not restated). -->
    <dependency>
      <groupId>org.flexdock</groupId>
      <artifactId>flexdock</artifactId>
      <version>1.2.5</version>
      <scope>system</scope>
      <systemPath>${project.basedir}/../../thirdparty/flexdock-1.2.5.jar</systemPath>
    </dependency>
    <!-- JEDITERM CORE — com.jediterm.core.util.TermSize
         (PtyTtyConnector.java:16), com.jediterm.terminal.TtyConnector
         (PtyTtyConnector.java:17), com.jediterm.terminal.
         TerminalExecutorServiceManager (ScilabTerminal.java:44). Real
         coordinate `org.jetbrains.jediterm:jediterm-core:3.70`, sourced from
         fetch-thirdparty.sh's own MAVEN_MANIFEST (JetBrains' own
         intellij-dependencies repository, not Central) — see this file's
         header comment. -->
    <dependency>
      <groupId>org.jetbrains.jediterm</groupId>
      <artifactId>jediterm-core</artifactId>
      <version>3.70</version>
      <scope>system</scope>
      <systemPath>${project.basedir}/../../thirdparty/jediterm-core-3.70.jar</systemPath>
    </dependency>
    <!-- JEDITERM UI — com.jediterm.terminal.ui.JediTermWidget
         (ScilabTerminal.java:45), com.jediterm.terminal.ui.settings.
         {DefaultSettingsProvider, SettingsProvider} (ScilabTerminal.java:46-47).
         A SEPARATE jar from jediterm-core (verified per-class: `unzip -l` shows
         JediTermWidget/DefaultSettingsProvider/SettingsProvider live here, not
         in -core) — system scope is never transitive, so both are declared.
         Real coordinate `org.jetbrains.jediterm:jediterm-ui:3.70`, same source
         as jediterm-core above. -->
    <dependency>
      <groupId>org.jetbrains.jediterm</groupId>
      <artifactId>jediterm-ui</artifactId>
      <version>3.70</version>
      <scope>system</scope>
      <systemPath>${project.basedir}/../../thirdparty/jediterm-ui-3.70.jar</systemPath>
    </dependency>
    <!-- JNA — com.sun.jna.{Library, Memory, Native, Pointer, StringArray} and
         com.sun.jna.ptr.IntByReference (Pty.java:16-21), the native PTY bridge.
         Real Maven Central coordinate `net.java.dev.jna:jna:5.14.0`, sourced
         from fetch-thirdparty.sh's own MAVEN_MANIFEST — see this file's header
         comment. -->
    <dependency>
      <groupId>net.java.dev.jna</groupId>
      <artifactId>jna</artifactId>
      <version>5.14.0</version>
    </dependency>
  </dependencies>

  <build>
    <!-- build.incl.xml:22 <property name="src.dir" location="src/java/"/>.
         Same source tree Ant compiles — see modules/localization/pom.xml's
         identical comment; nothing module-specific to add here. -->
    <sourceDirectory>src/java</sourceDirectory>

    <plugins>
      <plugin>
        <groupId>org.apache.maven.plugins</groupId>
        <artifactId>maven-jar-plugin</artifactId>
        <configuration>
          <archive>
            <!-- addMavenDescriptor=false and the Built-By entry are inherited
                 from the parent POM — not redeclared here. Same manifestFile
                 mechanism as modules/localization/pom.xml (see that file's
                 build comment for the full rationale). MANIFEST-section.MF's
                 bytes were EXTRACTED from the actual Ant-built jar's
                 META-INF/MANIFEST.MF, never retyped — see this file's header
                 comment for the full manifest rationale (double-mangled vendor
                 string, frozen Implementation-Version, uninterpolated
                 Class-Path literal). -->
            <manifestFile>${project.basedir}/src/main/manifest/MANIFEST-section.MF</manifestFile>
          </archive>
        </configuration>
      </plugin>
    </plugins>
  </build>
</project>
